Chapter: Fat16List
  cites Foreword chapter Fat16

 A listing with no disk attached returns the empty list, so a correct
 implementation and a broken one are indistinguishable without a disk. This
 test attaches one: fat16-list.disk is a GPT image whose FAT16 ESP holds
 CODEX.CDX in the root and BOOTX64.EFI inside EFI/BOOT, so it pins the
 root listing, the subdirectory walk, the file/directory split and the
 extension filter against bytes that are really there.

 It also pins the two answers that were wrong. file-exists returned False
 for every path on every disk, because it guarded on block-sector-count,
 which reads 0 on a disk that is attached and reads perfectly. And the
 guard it replaces cannot simply be dropped: with no disk the boot record
 parses out of zeroes, bytes-per-sector is 0, and the root-directory size
 divides by it. fat16-init is total now and the volume itself says whether
 it is usable.

 We say:

Section: Reporting

  show-list : Text, List Text, Integer, Integer -> [Console] Nothing
  show-list (label) (xs) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then act print-line-uni (label & " end") end
    else act
      print-line-uni (label & " " & list-at xs i)
      show-list label xs (i + 1) n
    end

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console, Device.Block] Nothing
  opening = act
    hit <- file-exists "CODEX.CDX"
    print-line-uni ("exists-present " & show hit)
    miss <- file-exists "NOPE.XXX"
    print-line-uni ("exists-absent " & show miss)
    dirs <- list-directories ""
    show-list "rootdir" dirs 0 (list-length dirs)
    files <- list-files "" ""
    show-list "rootfile" files 0 (list-length files)
    boot <- list-files "EFI/BOOT" ""
    show-list "bootfile" boot 0 (list-length boot)
    cdx <- list-files "" ".CDX"
    show-list "extfilter" cdx 0 (list-length cdx)
    nope <- list-files "" ".ZZZ"
    show-list "extnomatch" nope 0 (list-length nope)
  end
